59d7e6351fb4409075ec4bdc7bef6","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-hn.1/state.json","size_bytes":213}},"finished_at":"2026-11-05T23:57:01.004902+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-hn.1","local_name":"bob-cli-hn.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-hn","agent_clan_generation":"20261105184352","bead_id":"bob-cli-hn.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-hn[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Successor card verdicts — mark offers Done or Cancel from the card[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]While reviewing a successor card in Obsidian, in Bob Mac Capture, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]or through `bob capture`, Bryan can stage Done (Ctrl+X) or Cancel [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim](Ctrl+Shift+X, with an optional inline reason) on any eligible [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]offer row. Those verdicts apply together with pull-ins in the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]gesture's existing write pass. The engine reports eligibility and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]consequences, closes are root-only, cascades are recover-only, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]failures are reported honestly, and the card uses Bob's existing [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]✓/⊘ visual grammar.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]9[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]successor_card_verdicts.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-hn[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-hn/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Contract, vectors table, and decision record[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract: write the binding bob-cli docs contract in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs/task-dependencies.md §12.22–12.23 and the §12.5/§12.13/§12.14 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]additions (the SV vector table, canonical copy, CLI/JSON/API shapes), [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plus the memory changes the accepted decisions authorize.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust offer-close engine and per-row close descriptors[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]engine[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]engine: build the pure Rust offer-close engine (eligibility, root-only [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Done, Task-Card-parity Cancel, recover-only cascade, consequence copy), [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]attach a `close` descriptor to every capture offer row, and publish [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tests/fixtures/offer_close/vectors.json.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob capture -x/-X flags, batch post-pass, and receipts[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli: add `-x/--complete-offer` and `-X/--cancel-offer`, resolve and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]validate verdicts, apply them in a capture post-pass, and emit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]offer.verdict, pull_in.close, offer_closes[], refusals, human output, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]help, completion, and docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Obsidian successor picker verdict UI (api.successors v4)[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-card[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-card: add per-row verdict state, keys, the inline cancel reason, the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]visuals, footer, two-step Esc, and hover buttons to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SuccessorOfferPickerModal, and bump api.successors to v4 with the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]{picks, closes} result.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Nav cancel API v1 and Unblocked notice v4[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-apis[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-card[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-apis: expose a pure Task-Card-parity cancel planner as api.cancel [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]v1, and extend api.notice to v4 with offer-close rows, refusal lines, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tickler lines, and a guarded Undo action.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Cycler eligibility, verdict apply step, receipts, and undo[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]cycler[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine, nav-apis[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cycler: compute close descriptors that match the shared vectors, attach [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]them when nav v4 is present, apply returned closes in a guarded verdict [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]step with recover-only cascades, send receipts with Undo restores, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pin the walk and reopen rules.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Verdicts on the Obsidian project-promotion card[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]promotion[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cycler[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]promotion: expose the cycler's describe/apply offer-close functions as [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cycler api v5 and wire them into nav's project-promotion successor card.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]The task-merge card stays pull-in-only.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]CaptureCore decoding, outcome model, argv, and fixtures[/b